# Infinigrams

A React-based Nonogram game (also known as Picross or Paint by Numbers). Fill cells from numerical hints to reveal a hidden picture — generate endless random puzzles, or turn your photos into puzzles.

## Features

- Grid sizes from 5×5 to 20×20
- Easy / Medium / Hard difficulty
- Drag-to-fill and right-click to mark empty cells (X)
- Victory wave animation and live timer
- Seed-based puzzles for sharing
- Photo-to-nonogram generation with live preview

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+
- npm

### Installation

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

Open the URL Vite prints (usually `http://localhost:5173/infinigrams/`).

## Scripts

| Command | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run dev` | Start the Vite dev server |
| `npm run build` | Typecheck and build for production |
| `npm run preview` | Preview the production build |
| `npm run deploy` | Deploy `dist/` to GitHub Pages |

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/           # UI components
│   ├── GameBoard.tsx
│   ├── DifficultySelector.tsx
│   ├── SizeSelector.tsx
│   ├── PhotoUploader.tsx
│   └── GameSetup.tsx
├── stores/
│   └── gameStore.ts      # Zustand game state
├── types/
│   └── gameTypes.ts
└── utils/
    ├── puzzleGenerator.ts
    ├── imageProcessor.ts
    ├── solverUtils.ts
    ├── debounce.ts
    └── timeUtils.ts
```

## How to Play

1. Choose a grid size and difficulty, or upload a photo
2. Use the row/column hints to decide which cells to fill
3. Controls:
   - Left click/drag to fill cells
   - Right click/drag to mark empty cells with X
   - Click filled cells again to mark with X
   - Click X-marked cells to clear them
4. Fill every correct cell to win

## Technologies

- React 18
- TypeScript
- Vite
- Tailwind CSS
- Zustand
- seedrandom (reproducible puzzles)
